# Cordova plugins for Capacitor
capacitor-cordova-ios-plugins

# Generated Config files
App/App/capacitor.config.json
App/App/config.xml

# THE SPM MANIFEST IS GENERATED TOO, AND FOR A SHARPER REASON THAN THE TWO
# ABOVE. ci_post_clone.sh runs `npx cap sync ios` on every build, and sync
# REWRITES CapApp-SPM/Package.swift whatever is committed. So a tracked copy
# is overwritten before it is ever compiled: it can never be load-bearing,
# and can only be stale, wrong, or a confusing diff.
#
# It was tracked until 29 Aug 2026, and it was WRONG — generated once by
# `cap add ios` before any plugin existed, naming only Capacitor and Cordova.
# @capacitor/browser and @capacitor/app were added later and nothing
# regenerated it, so build 7 shipped with a Browser plugin that had no native
# half. Untracking it removes the whole class rather than that one instance.
#
# AND DO NOT REGENERATE IT ON WINDOWS AND COMMIT THE RESULT. The CLI builds
# these paths with path.relative and interpolates them raw
# (@capacitor/cli/dist/util/spm.js:140), so on Windows it writes backslashes:
# separators into that path. In Swift source those are escape sequences and
# the file does not parse at all.
# sequences and the file does not parse.
App/CapApp-SPM/Package.swift
